{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0791a1593bc7a07e87bc2e7a4640bf057ebd1b02383bc948434e9c3d26d8dd74","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan review attestation classification","key_entities":["classify_plan_review_attestation","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py","ATTESTATION_SIDECAR_LOST","sidecar_emitted","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json","sign-review","review-plan"],"problem_keywords":["attestation failure","recovery guidance","sidecar persistence","stale verdict","misleading error message"],"propositions":["When review-plan PASSES but attestation write fails due to lock timeout, the error message advises running sign-review, which cannot work if the PASS sidecar was also lost.","The sidecar_emitted field exists on the result dict but is never inspected in classify_plan_review_attestation's catch-all branch that handles sign failures.","When both sidecar and signature are lost, the system retains the previous round's BLOCK verdict as current, creating a stale contradictory state that persists even after the failed review.","A new ATTESTATION_SIDECAR_LOST classification with recovery_tool=review_plan is needed to distinguish sidecar-lost failures from sign-only failures and provide correct recovery guidance."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787770861229946001,"uuid":"dd869949-24ff-4f62-bc76-e3e7cbdab3a8"}